  "tags": [
    {
      "name": "Login",
      "description": "SSPA will expose a set of APIs which will be utilized by BAFL to perform beneficiary  \nverification/validation, account status update (whenever account status changes), credits  \nand debits reporting. The communication between BAFL and SSPA will be done over a  \nsecure VPN channel\n\n**Request Body**  \n{  \n\"Username\": \"string (max 30)\",  \n\"Password\": \"string (max 30)\"\n\n}"
    },
    {
      "name": "Inquiry",
      "description": "When beneficiary approaches BAFL BVS Agent for Opening the LMA and/or withdrawal  \npayment, BAFL will need an API from SSPA to verify whether she is an active beneficiary and  \nif she has an already opened account or not, and retrieve other pertinent details (due  \namount, mobile number, request ID).  \nScenario: When a beneficiary approaches a BAFL BVS agent to open an LMA account or  \nwithdraw a payment, BAFL will call SSPA\u2019s Beneficiary Inquiry API to:  \n\u2022 Verify whether the CNIC is an active SSPA beneficiary  \n\u2022 Determine if an LMA account is already opened  \n\u2022 Retrieve the beneficiary\u2019s due amount, mobile number, enrollment date, and unique  \nrequest identifier  \nThis check ensures BAFL enforces eligibility and proceeds only for valid beneficiaries  \nBusiness Rules at Account Opening and Credit Stage:  \n\u2022 Age (18 to 49) \u2013 to be calculated from the time of enrolment with SSPA  \n\u2022 Gender (Female)  \n\u2022 Maximum amount 30,000/beneficiary  \n\u2022 If payment amount returned from SSPA is \u20180\u2019 (zero) \u2013 account will be opened  \nwith no credit to account.  \n\u2022 CNIC expiry"
    },
    {
      "name": "Account Opening Update",
      "description": "After a beneficiary\u2019s LMA account is opened at a BAFL BVS agent or through Bulk or through  \nBAFL Branch, BAFL system will call SSPA\u2019s Account Opening Update API to share the newly  \nassigned IBAN/Account Number along with associated beneficiary details. SSPA uses this  \ninformation to reconcile its records and enable subsequent payment processing.  \nBAFL will create and share a code-based district and tehsil library with their mapping IDs  \nfrom their system, in order to map the IDs with SSPA. This will enable the APIs to exchange  \nonly district and tehsil codes instead of names, to avoid mismatch of multiple permutations.  \nBusiness Rules to be Enforced  \n\u2022 IBAN_No and Account No. is the primary key and must be unique and non-null  \n\u2022 CNIC_No forms a composite key with IBAN_No and must be non-null  \n\u2022 Mobile_No must be unique across all records  \n\u2022 BVS_sessionID is mandatory for accounts opened via BVS POS  \n\u2022 CNIC_Issuance_Date, Beneficiary_Name, and Processing_Mode are mandatory"
    },
    {
      "name": "Credit Reporting LMA",
      "description": "BAFL will report all credits into a beneficiary\u2019s LMA in real time via SSPA\u2019s Credit Reporting  \nAPI. Each report includes SSPA payment details, credit amount, transaction identifiers, and  \nupdated balance. This will enable SSPA to maintain an accurate, up-to-date ledger of  \nbeneficiary account activity.\n\n**Business Rules & Constraints:**  \n\u2022 Composite Primary Key: CNIC_No + Transaction_No  \n\u2022 Unique Constraint: BAFL_TransactionNo + SSPA_Request_ID  \n\u2022 Foreign Key: IBAN and Account No. references AccountDetail table  \n\u2022 CNIC_No, Transaction_Type, IBAN, Account No, Payment_Channel,  \nSSPA_Request_ID, Transaction_No, Credit_Amount, Balance, and  \nTransaction_Time are non-null  \n\u2022 Request_Transaction_Id is posted by SSPA when provided; otherwise, BAFL  \ngenerates it for any reversals"
    },
    {
      "name": "Withdrawal Reporting",
      "description": "BAFL will report beneficiary withdrawal on real time basis, which will include the withdrawal  \ndetails like channel (Agent/ATM/Branch), amount, agent details, transaction details, geo  \nlocation (for validation of 50-meter radius), and withdrawal device IMEI/MAC ID/Serial No.  \netc.  \nSSPA will expose the API that will be utilized by BAFL to update beneficiary account activity.  \nAll essential details will be saved.  \nBAFL will create and share a code-based district and tehsil library with their mapping IDs  \nfrom their system, in order to map the IDs with SSPA. This will enable the APIs to exchange  \nonly district and tehsil codes instead of names, to avoid mismatch of multiple permutations.  \nBusiness Rules to be Enforced:  \n\u2022 NADRA\u2019s BVS_session_ID & Account_Type is a new unique constraint  \n\u2022 Foreign key is Account No of BAFL from Account Detail table.  \n\u2022 Whitelisting of BVS Agent with SSPA system is prerequisite for report of  \nWithdrawal.  \n\u2022 Reporting of channel (BVS/ATM) for each withdrawal whether 1st time or  \nrecurrent withdrawal.  \n\u2022 IMEI or MAC ID or Serial No. of agent device will be pushed  \n\u2022 CNIC No. and Transaction No. is composite PK  \n\u2022 CNIC No. is FK from account detail  \n\u2022 CNIC No. is not null  \n\u2022 Withdrawal Channel is not null  \n\u2022 IBAN and Account Number is not null  \n\u2022 BVS Agent ID / ATM ID is not Null  \n\u2022 Transaction Type is not null  \n\u2022 Amount is not null  \n\u2022 Transaction Time is not null  \n\u2022 NADRA\u2019s_Session_ID is not null  \n\u2022 NADRA\u2019s_Session_ID is unique"
    },
    {
      "name": "Withdrawal Reporting Point",
      "description": "This API to allow BAFL to register or update its BVS touchpoints\u2014including  \nBVS Agents, BVS ATMs, and Branches\u2014prior to initiating live account opening and  \ntransaction workflows. Each touchpoint must be mapped to a valid district, tehsil, and union  \ncouncil using BAFL\u2019s address library (shared with SSPA). This ensures traceability and geo  \nvalidation across all beneficiary interactions.\n\n  \n**Business Rules & Constraints:**  \n\u2022 Register all operational locations with SSPA before activation  \n\u2022 Enable SSPA to associate transactions with verified BAFL touchpoints  \n\u2022 Enforce geo-coordinates and address integrity for audit and compliance  \n\u2022 Date wise history will be maintained of any updates and/or previous records in both  \nBAFL and SSPA DBs ."
    },
    {
      "name": "Transaction Log",
      "description": "This API for BAFL to post real-time logs of all transaction attempts related  \nto SSPA business, including successful operations, declines, BVS errors, network or system  \nfailures, and missing acknowledgments. BAFL must call this endpoint for each transaction  \nattempt (up to five BVS retries), supplying context and error details for audit and monitoring.\n\n  \n**Reporting Rules:**  \n\u2022 Log every transaction attempt (success or failure) with BAFL session ID  \n\u2022 Include all BVS retry attempts and their outcomes  \n\u2022 Report declines, BVS errors, system/network failures, and missing  \nacknowledgments  \n\u2022 Associate each log entry with the original API name and correlation ID for  \ntraceability"
    }
  ]
}